  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Fire Management Hub (Multidonor Facility)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The idea of the Global Fire Management Hub (Fire Hub for short), was announced by FAO Senior Management at the XV World Forestry Congress, welcomed by FAO Members during the 26th session of the Committee on Forestry in October 2022 and officially launched during the 8th International Wildland Fire Conference (IWFC) in May 2023.
The primary aim of the Fire Hub and this project is to enhance countries? capacities to implement Integrated Fire Management (IFM), significantly reducing the adverse impacts of wildfires on communities, landscapes, and global climate. The Fire Hub will provide a ?one stop shop? for knowledge on IFM, information on current global fire situation, and activities of the international fire community.</narrative>
  </description>
